  tuples exactly tile the input range, with small, odd, and real
  RELSEG_SIZE values.  A >1 GiB end-to-end test is impractical, so the
  splitting arithmetic -- where a wrong byte range would corrupt data --
  is covered deterministically here instead.


Limitations
-----------

* Only completely empty, non-all-visible pages whose LSN predates the
  last completed checkpoint are punched; anything else keeps the stock
  behavior.
* Reclaimed space is filesystem blocks only; the logical relation size
  never shrinks (unlike truncation).
* Best-effort by design: unsupported platforms/filesystems silently do
  nothing, and skipped pages are simply left for a future vacuum.
